      <orbit:note>You can now see icons next to commands in the Windows command bar, plus favicons on page results and a Tab key badge on the site search row.</orbit:note>
      <orbit:note>Right-clicking an image, link, selected text or text field now shows Inspect at the bottom of the menu.</orbit:note>
      <orbit:note>Typing the start of a site you've visited now completes its home page, even when busy article pages from that site rank higher.</orbit:note>
      <orbit:note>The Windows space bar now has larger, hover-responsive buttons with dots, icons and emoji sized like the Mac's, and Downloads and Archive sit at the left.</orbit:note>
      <orbit:note>Creating a new live folder, or turning a folder into one, no longer freezes the app for a moment.</orbit:note>
      <orbit:note>Collapsing a section, folder or space in the sidebar now slides each row's title along with its icon instead of jumping.</orbit:note>
      <orbit:note>You can now rename and delete profiles, move spaces between profiles on the Mac, and deleting a profile removes its logins and data.</orbit:note>
      <orbit:note>Searching the command bar for "connect google" no longer shows unrelated rows like Changelog and GitHub token sign-in.</orbit:note>
      <orbit:note>You can now copy an entire scrollable page to the clipboard as one image with Capture Full Page, using View ▸ Capture, ⌘⌥2, or the command bar.</orbit:note>
      <orbit:note>VoiceOver can now reach the capture bar and its Copy, Cancel and Add to Easel buttons when you select a page region.</orbit:note>
